{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383401-mage-manila-just-bouncing-ideas","id":1383401,"title":"Mage Manila, just bouncing ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-23T11:01:37-07:00","id":1383401,"title":"Mage Manila, just bouncing ideas","content":"I'm back. I was kept away from this site by reality. Anyway, I'm currently making some material for Mage games set in the Philippines (Because I love Mage and live in the Philippines). Though I don't know when I'll be done, I was hoping to bounce some ideas off you people. <br /> <br /> Currently, I've made 9 NPC tradition Mages who are supposed to be establishing a major tradition chantry in Manila. Sort of a multi-tradition school, library, and designated survivor bunker for a just in case leadership gets wiped out again. I'm making a counterpart set of 10 Technocracy NPCs who work in Manila recruiting awakened mages and other people who might be of help to the technocracy. Later on, Implant to make a Tradition mage adventure involving the creation of the chantry, a Technocracy adventure and some epic Adventure involving Bakunawa, the moon eating dragon. Im hoping to eventually make more stuff. Not even sure how to show this stuff to people. Thanks in advance for any input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T15:26:18-07:00","id":1383455,"title":"","content":"For the polished work, the Storyteller's Vault would be a good place to put your work.<br /> <br /> The Traditions chantry could be one short book. With 9 NPCs and a write-up of the chantry and a little on Manilla, it could be something for other Storytellers to use directly, or to take pieces of for use in their game (like a chantry description, map of the chantry or NPCs).<br /> <br /> The Technocracy Construct and its 10 NPCs could be another book.<br /> <br /> Then, your adventures could each be another book or a three-pack connecting all adventures.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where you are at in the writing, but with the Technocracy: Reloaded book scheduled to hit Kickstarter on April 28, or 5 days from now, you might want to have the Technocracy material ready soon to coincide with the wave of interest in the Technocracy that Kickstarter will generate.<br /> <br /> There are several ways to share your work before it is final<br /> 1. Forum threads<br /> 2. Google Drive (set editing permissions careful)<br /> 3. Dropbox<br /> 4. In a Discord group or some other chat service with document sharing.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend you be clear on what type of feedback you're looking for and what are the areas which need the most feedback. Fans can be great playtesters, but I have found in helping with playtests and doing rules work for other games that you can spend a lot of time on corner cases and on trying to develop very specific phrasings and language instead of letting the game move on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T17:06:54-07:00","id":1383472,"title":"","content":"Thanks. That really helps. I'll look into the Storyteller's vault once I finish and polish the two NPC books and get some positive user feedback. I had roughly your idea for the book divisions but did not think to make a chantry/construct write-up for each. <br /> <br /> As for what feedback I'm looking for right now, I'm wondering what other sorts of things people might look for when running or playing Mage in the Philippines setting. Like what would most interest them. Like, more Adventures? More NPCs? Wonders? Specific location stuff?<br /> <br /> I'd try to make what I can of these things. It's all for fun really. While work takes up much of my time, it seems my leisure time gets spent on stuff like this and, I like how it's coming so far.<br /> <br /> As for feedback on what I'm currently writing, I guess I'll fix up all those NPCs on both sides first so that they can kinda be taken as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T21:33:56-07:00","id":1383504,"title":"","content":"Well, since I'm from the U.S. and only know about the Philippines in small chunks where it intersects with U.S. history, to run a series of adventures there or a chronicle there, I'd be looking for more location-specific information.<br /> <br /> While I appreciate crunch and rules elements, Mage is so much everyone's individual game ruleswise that it's harder to balance crunch. Good fluff, or details about things I can use will help.<br /> <br /> Maybe something like the 'By Night' series for Vampire would be helpful to introduce the Philippines. You could have some short adventures there as well.<br /> <br /> However, that's just one vote. If there's a way to start a poll, consider what you can write and would like to write and put up a poll with those options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T02:02:47-07:00","id":1383536,"title":"","content":"Ahoy my Pinoy brother. The Philippines would be an interesting position of being a border territory of the East and West, much like India, or even Hong Kong. Supernatural phenomena that would catch the attention of mages could be Wan Gui Flesh Shintai users being the local Manananggal. And various local Changelings/Diwatas. The Naga/Marinaga already could represented by two mermaid Kiths.<br /> <br /> Bakunawa would make a perfect example of one of the Wani Dragon Princes, as the various godlike Dragons seem to make up their membership.<br /> <br /> Wakwak could be Corax/Tengu of the region.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting to explore say the relationship between the Catholic and Muslim Celestial Choristers of the city. I can see Dreamspeakers,Verbena and Etherites exploring relationships with the local Fae beings.<br /> <br /> I am curious on your ideas of things like how the local consensus works. Like superstitions and folkloric traditions are pretty alive in the Philippines and I would translate that to easier time not triggering paradox when evoking things like ghost stories and the like.<br /> <br /> How many of the Mages are local, all of them? Are any of them Foreign? Same with the Technocrats. I can see the Five Elemental Dragons (the Eastern Technocracy Subbranch) competing to suborn influence in the face of the Five Metal Dragons (Western Technocracy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T02:30:11-07:00","id":1383541,"title":"","content":"Re. Vault material for the Phillipines maybe have a chat to Dion Fernandez who has written three Phillipines based books for the Storytellers Vault.<br /> <br /> I'm currently playing a Mage chronicle where my PC is a <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mangkukulam masquerading as an Albularyo.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T04:04:36-07:00","id":1383550,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13680_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13680\" data-vbnamecard=\"13680\">baakyocalder</a>. That's a great idea. Not sure I can write a Manila &quot;by night&quot; for Mage properly but I guess I'll give it a try. But definitely, what I'll make will focus more on location and setting lore than crunch. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a>. Yo, hi! In terms of consensus, it should be fairly permissive as Filipinos tend not to really care absolutely exactly how things work so long as they work. Meaning, some of the tamer magic stuff all around will be coincidental, like faith healing disease, but not wounds or anything too visibly obvious. Inversely some tech that would normally break down in the deep wilderness will still function here. Then there's local lore like ghost stories and against and such.<br /> <br /> As for the mages I've made, two are locals, a dreamspeaker katalonan and a chorus exorcist. The akashic was born elsewhere but was already living in the Philippines. The rest are foreigners. This is mainly because I'm planning to feature more local characters in the adventures and figure it would be nicer to have some of the tradition people discovering the Philippines alongside foreign players. I'm still coming up with the Tech, but many of them will be from the country as the Technocracy has been actively recruiting from the country for some time now. Not sure how to approach the metal dragons yet. I was thinking of putting one in the Tech team actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T04:05:34-07:00","id":1383551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383401-mage-manila-just-bouncing-ideas?p=1383541#post1383541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re. Vault material for the Phillipines maybe have a chat to Dion Fernandez who has written three Phillipines based books for the Storytellers Vault.<br /> <br /> I'm currently playing a Mage chronicle where my PC is a <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mangkukulam masquerading as an Albularyo.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. I'll see if I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T10:50:04-07:00","id":1383628,"title":"","content":"Random thoughts.<br /> <br /> Tradition-wise, I'm guessing that what would eventually become part of the Dreamspeakers would be the oldest established faction in the islands, dating back to the pre-iron age peoples who've been there since at least around 2000BC. My (admitted limited) understanding of this period is that these peoples had linguistic and genetic connections with various Pacific Island peoples, including Polynesians, so it's possible there may be Kopa Loei groups in the Philippines going back that far as well. The modern Dreamspeakers are undoubtably as diverse here as they are everywhere else, ranging from ultra-traditionalist shaman and Catholic syncretist faith healers to modern storytellers using Pinoy manga as a medium to keep old stories alive and techno-shaman oceanographers studying sea-dwelling spirits and bygones. <br /> <br /> Maritime trade with the various kingdoms of Southeast Asia and China very likely brought Thanatoics and Akashics to the islands. I'm not knowledgable enough to guess what Thanatoics of that period would've been like, but there's probably been two other influxes of them during the American colonial period and the wave of immigrants who came from Sindhi after the 1947 partition of India and Pakistan. My understanding is that most of them are middle class merchants and financiers, so I could easily see the Lhaksmists being one of the main factions. The Akashics are probably a mix of various native ethnic groups (including their cultures and traditions as gateway arts to Do), Chinese, and later Japanese cultures, as well as all of the other groups more modernist Akashics associate with. Chinese immigration, especially in the past century or so, has probably also brought with it members of the Wu Lung and the Wu Keng. <br /> <br /> Muslim traders and the influx of both missionaries and refugees from the Portuguese and Dutch conquest of Malaysia and Indonesia brought Islam, especially to the south, and very likely the Ahl I Batin with it. Just as my personal head canon, I have placed the Philippines as the eastern most edge of the Web of Faith network prior to it getting badly damaged in the 20th century. I suspect there are still Batini covertly lurking around the country. <br /> <br /> The Spanish conquest and colonization certainly brought members of the Celestial Chorus. They've probably been as active with various syncretist groups as they are with more traditional Catholics. Another source of Chorus history in the Philippines could be the Japanese kirishitan, the Catholic Japanese who sought sanctuary in the islands during the 17th century Tokugawa purges. It's a culture that mostly died out, but makes an interesting bit of Tradition history, IMO. <br /> The Spanish also probably brought the Order of Hermes with them. Given their traditional ties with Iberia, I can easily see a number of House Flambeau as the forefront of their arrival. Probably also the more tactful members of House Jerbiton as well. They've probably got at least one chantry dating back to the early 17th century, thought it's entirely possible it could've been destroyed during WW2 or some other point. <br /> <br /> And, obviously, the modern world has certainly seen Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts in the nation as well. Unfortunately, I don't know enough about modern Filipino culture to even guess if the Hollow Ones would have a niche there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T10:58:47-07:00","id":1383630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383401-mage-manila-just-bouncing-ideas?p=1383472#post1383472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what feedback I'm looking for right now, I'm wondering what other sorts of things people might look for when running or playing Mage in the Philippines setting. Like what would most interest them. Like, more Adventures? More NPCs? Wonders? Specific location stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Anything about local mystical traditions (both old and new), including what sort of tools/foci they'd use and Rotes.</li> <li>Talismans/Wonders, especially anything unique to the region, such as objects of local mythology and folklore (including modern urban legends).</li> <li>Native Bygones.</li> <li>Local folk beliefs, urban legends, superstitions, historical mysteries, social taboos and the sort of things you never really see in guide books or travel documentaries. I find these make good plot hooks.</li> <li>Places that might make for cool or interesting nodes or other places of power.</li> <li>Local subcultures that PCs might be a part of. (Again, this is one of those things that is sometimes hard for outsiders to find.)</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T15:58:38-07:00","id":1383680,"title":"","content":"Book partially on 'Crafts' of the islands detailing things like forms of <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Pagkukulam throughout the Phillipines, Glossary of Terms and definitions, relations with the Aswang Courts ( ( One of my favourite sites: </span></span></span><a href=\"https://www.aswangproject.com/creatures-mythical-beings-philippine-folklore-mythology/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.aswangproject.com/creatu...ore-mythology/</a> ), Rotes and Practices all the good stuff.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T10:15:23-07:00","id":1383788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383401-mage-manila-just-bouncing-ideas?p=1383628#post1383628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And, obviously, the modern world has certainly seen Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts in the nation as well. Unfortunately, I don't know enough about modern Filipino culture to even guess if the Hollow Ones would have a niche there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your random thoughts are actually a great help. <br /> <br /> As for the local sons of ether, they tend to focus on creating cutting edge tech that can be constructed without the need for overly expensive and complex infrastructure. Things like medical incubators made of bamboo, cheap aquaponic urban vertical gardens with plastic &quot;fish tanks&quot; as a water source, mango yield tripling chemicals, coconut cellulose burn patches, and artificial wood made from agricultural waste. Agriculture and the use of natural ingredients or recycled materials seem to be their thing.<br /> <br /> Despite truly terrible internet infrastructure, virtual adepts thrive in the Philippines, a place where even some of the poorest urban kids can access the internet on a phone or at a low cost internet shop.<br /> <br /> I'm not an expert at hollow ones but the Philippines does have a goth rock scene, punk bands, hip hop culture, and such... So they must be around somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T10:19:34-07:00","id":1383791,"title":"","content":"I guess most of the stuff I'm making after the first batch will be location based adventures with some NPCs and whatever local totes, bygones, mystic locations, wonders, groups etc. Need to be detailed within them. Currently doing the Technocracy Philippine recruitment center NPCs. Probably located in Makati","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T10:44:55-07:00","id":1383794,"title":"","content":"I was thinking biotech, as well as trying to bridge the gap between Matter and Life, might be one of the hot new trends among the current generation of Etherites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T14:01:56-07:00","id":1383839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383401-mage-manila-just-bouncing-ideas?p=1383794#post1383794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking biotech, as well as trying to bridge the gap between Matter and Life, might be one of the hot new trends among the current generation of Etherites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Philippine Genetically Modified and Genetically Engineered plant and animal rules are pretty permissive here I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T22:12:49-07:00","id":1383907,"title":"","content":"For the Hollow Ones, I would imagine two forces would be at play to influence how it shakes out.<br /> <br /> First, of course, is how natives interpret western Romantic ideas. I can't begin to guess how, but it's inevitable that when ideas are adopted, they do so through a local cultural lens.<br /> <br /> Second is that, aside from those Gothic and Romantic ideas that filter in through western media and cultural osmosis, if native Hollow Ones identify as such, that means they've been in contact with the larger Craft. Though that could just mean specific individuals or small groups. Depending on how such interactions go, the local Hollow One philosophical landscape may be heavily informed by the idiosyncrasies and fixations of a <i>specific mage</i> from the Craft.<br /> <br /> (To use another cultural example, Aleister Crowley and the Golden Dawn - in the latter case, specifically those members who broke secrecy - were the public's main gateway into western occultism. Their fixations and philosophies became ingrained into the philosophical zeitgeist, whether they were present in the larger body of occult theory before or not. To the point where ideas like Crowley's fixation on Will being <i>back-ported</i> to Hermeticism as a whole, once the Order of Hermes as a fictional entity in Mage and Ars Magicka came into being. HOW ideas got to a region is as important to the development of subcultures as what those ideas are, as their context and connotations can be flavored by the telling.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T23:57:34-07:00","id":1386627,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm back. It took much longer than I thought it would, but here is what I came up with for some Mage Manila characters.<br /> Traditions:<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zp28vbdiR9Gz7e8R70fPcDvScMzEWcr3/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zp2...ScMzEWcr3/view</a><br /> Technocracy:<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fHmNg_fk4Oqei8Lz0ao_URDeBCgI-hJy/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fHm...eBCgI-hJy/view</a><br /> I hope these links work<br /> <br /> I also have a link for these on my blog - <a href=\"https://godegeekery.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://godegeekery.wordpress.com/</a> - but a lot of these (blog posts) are unrelated to the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Comments and suggestions are very welcome.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are typos and inconsistencies here and there. I wrote the rotes/adjustments the way I did as a quick guide for my use if I were to run a game with these characters and the format was meant for whan i run games on my laptop.<br /> <br /> As I might have mentioned earlier (I'm not sure if I did, to be honest), I'm planning to make a few Adventures for mage set in the Philippines, the first of which is a Tradition game of establishing a Council Chantry in Intramuros which will probably involve doing something about the numerous spirits that have been haunting the place since WWII and interactions with some other things that would spoil the surprise if I mentioned them. For the Traditions, most are not from the Philippines but are there because they have a good reason to be there. I plan to create more local Philippine mage NPCs in the Adentures themselves, as opposed to the Technocracy which will probably have more NPCs showing up from outside the country in their own adventures. I have to finish a bit of my own stuff before getting to these though, but woud love to hear about the sorts of adventures players might go for in a Philippine Mage game. I have no idea what I'll be doing for the Technocracy side of things quite yet.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, I think I'll make a new post to ask for comments since the title of this is somewhat off for that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":".  New post 05-08-2020, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}